<%= @section %>
# <%= @module %>

<!-- One paragraph: what this application does and for whom, in the words of VISION.md. -->

This part of the file is the application's own. The installer wrote it once and never rewrites it.

## Repo structure

| Path | What |
| --- | --- |
| `lib/<%= @app %>/` | the domain (`domain.ex`), the contracts in `contracts/`, their implementations, and the contexts |
| `lib/<%= @app %>_web/` | the web layer: the router, the controllers and components, the health plug |
| `priv/repo/migrations/` | Oban's migration, then the engine's and the verifier's, then the application's own |
| `config/runtime.exs` | the configuration in production, from the variables EHOS gives the application |
| `ehos.yaml` | what the application needs from EHOS, in the format EHOS defines |
| `test/` | the tests; `test/harness_test.exs` checks the docs |
| `docs/` | topic docs, one per area |
| `.claude/settings.json` | Claude Code's settings, which enable the `ehos-app` and `eh-os-contract` plugins and their skills |

## Where to read

| Area | Doc |
| --- | --- |
| What EHOS is, and what this application is for | [VISION.md](VISION.md) |
| The development cycle, running, building, deploying, upgrading | [DEVELOPMENT.md](DEVELOPMENT.md) |
| How a request flows, supervision, configuration, the image, decisions | [ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md) |
| Running and writing tests | [TESTING.md](TESTING.md) |
| Writing a domain or a contract | [lib/<%= @app %>/contracts/AGENTS.md](lib/<%= @app %>/contracts/AGENTS.md) |
| The web layer | [lib/<%= @app %>_web/AGENTS.md](lib/<%= @app %>_web/AGENTS.md)<%= if @phoenix_rules, do: ", and Phoenix's rules in [docs/phoenix.md](docs/phoenix.md)" %> |

A new topic doc goes in `docs/`, and gets a row here.

## Nested AGENTS.md files

- [lib/<%= @app %>/contracts/AGENTS.md](lib/<%= @app %>/contracts/AGENTS.md): the rules for
  writing a contract.
- [lib/<%= @app %>_web/AGENTS.md](lib/<%= @app %>_web/AGENTS.md): the web layer.

Each has a `CLAUDE.md` beside it that loads it: with a `CLAUDE.md` at the root, Claude Code reads
a nested `AGENTS.md` only through one. A new nested `AGENTS.md` gets its `CLAUDE.md`, and a line
here.

## Boundaries

<!-- What holds across the whole application, beyond EHOS's rules above, so that breaking it is a
design change rather than an implementation detail. -->

## Key patterns

- **A command** is declared in a contract, decided by its implementation, and dispatched by the
  engine, which appends what was decided to the event log.<%= if @example do %> The example is
  `lib/<%= @app %>/contracts/entries.ex`, implemented by `lib/<%= @app %>/entries/entry.ex` and
  served under `/api`.<% end %>
- **Configuration** that differs between environments comes from the variables EHOS gives the
  application, read in `config/runtime.exs`, never from a value written into the code.

## Gotchas

- A migration runs before the new release starts, so the old release must survive it: a drop
  ships in two deploys.
- `mix precommit` formats files and unlocks unused dependencies, so it is not a read-only check.

